WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
Привет, это Минц Хэлло и Нарашен.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.900
Привет русский, эпизод 52.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.440
Это 4th of July, 2026.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.540
Я, Олья, тадис Лесенн, will be a fun one.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.980
Поехали, our word of the day is дождь, дождь.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.680
Say, slowly with me.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.160
Дождь, дождь, Минц рейн.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.000
Эмажен дрезл, турнем into дождь.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.740
Войстарь с ним в дад софт, дей с саунд и бринген водор from the sky.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.320
Now repeat after me, дождь.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.620
Дождь, дождь, дождь, дождь, дождь, дождь, дождь.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.660
Это значит, it is raining.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.960
Тадис, мы are learning words to talk about the weather.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.720
Our next word is солнце, солнце.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.880
Солнце means sun, repeat after me, солнце.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.000
Here is a sentence.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.540
Солнце светит, солнце светит.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:46.680
The sun is shining.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.080
The memory hook works by linking солнце to the English word sun

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.680
with a cheerful Russian ending.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.860
Picture a big yellow ball smiling down from above.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.660
This helps your recall the word when you see bright light outside.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.840
Next comes snake, snake.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.340
Snack means snow.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:04.920
Repeat after me, snack.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:06.820
Say this sentence with me.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.600
Snack belly, snack belly.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.780
The snow is white.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.160
The memory hook connects snack to the word leg

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.920
because cold white flakes land on your leg.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.200
This image makes the term easier to keep in mind during winter months.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.380
Now we have ветер, ветер, ветер means wind.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.100
Repeat after me, ветер.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.320
Try this sentence, ветер do it, ветер do it,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.440
da wind is blowing.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.360
The memory hook compares ветер to ветером

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.880
because it describes air that has traveled far.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.200
This picture shows fast moving air in a simple way.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.320
Our next word is небо, небо, небо means sky.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.000
Repeat after me, небо.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.820
Here is how we use it, небо голубое, небо голубое,

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:48.800
доска из блю.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.160
Next is тепло, тепло, тепло means warm.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.700
Repeat after me, тепло.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.220
Listen to this sentence,

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.380
сегодня тепло, сегодня тепло.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:58.540
It is warm today.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.100
The memory hook ties тепло to teapet

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.160
because it means pleasant to warm weather.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.820
This link fits sunny days when the temperature feels comfortable.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.160
Our last new list is coldness, coldness.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:11.680
Coldness means cold.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.520
Repeat after me, coldness.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.960
Here is a sentence, зимой холодно, зимой холодно.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.120
It is cold in winter.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.020
The memory hook starts coldness with the same sound as cold.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.060
This makes it simple to remember on chilly days.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.120
Remember радуга from earlier.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.980
Радуга means rainbow.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.800
After the rain, we can say,

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.760
после дождя радуга, после дождя радуга.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.960
After the rain, there is a rainbow.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.480
The memory hook reminds you that радуга appears when sun meets rain.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.920
This shows how the word fits after a storm passes.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.500
You also know,

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.700
mой already, mой means my.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.520
We can say, mой дом,

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.200
mой дом, my house.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.280
The memory hook connects mой directly to the English word mой.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.940
This personal touch helps when describing your own weather view.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.620
Now, let's look at one small grammar idea.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.860
In Russian, adjective change your little to match the noun.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.440
Неба из нютер.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.340
So we say, глубое неба.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:09.720
Дождь is masculine,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.560
so we say, сильный дождь.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.640
The ending shows the match and makes the sentence sound right.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.540
English keeps adjectives the same for all nouns.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.460
Russian adds endings like oya or e to show agreement.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.480
This small change helps your sentences sound natural.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.080
Russians love talking about the weather.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.780
Winters are long and cold,

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.720
while summers can be hot and sunny.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.660
People often start a chat by asking him,

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.280
как погода, как погода.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.420
How is the weather?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.160
This question serves as a friendly greeting.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.420
It opens conversations in daily life.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.040
For our practice time, draw a picture of today's weather.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.180
Label the sun, rain, or snow with the Russian words.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.660
If you are looking out the window right now,

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.940
try saying, яркое и дместное подрезно,

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.780
благословечное Орское озеро.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.520
Then say, three times,

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:59.480
this activity helps fix the new terms in memory.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.140
Kids can use colors and shapes while adults can speak aloud.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.920
Want to know a secret about one of these words?

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.500
Did you know that the Russian word неба

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.640
and the English word небила are actually the same word?

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.840
They both come from the ancient Latin небила,

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.340
meaning cloud or mist.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.000
This word traveled through scientific writing

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.600
into English as небила for stary clouds.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.280
It stayed in Russian as the everyday word

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.520
for the sky above us,

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.380
but be careful.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.820
The Russian word неба also means heaven.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.820
Next time you look up at the sky,

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.020
remember неба,

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.380
it's cousins вид небуля.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.360
They both come from the same misty Latin root.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.660
That connection is your secret short,

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.140
cut to remembering it forever.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.660
You did great today.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.780
Say today's words out loud one more time and there yours.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.720
Share the show with a friend who wants to learn Russian

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.600
and I'll see you next time, пока.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.960
And if you'd rather watch it and listen,

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.240
find us on YouTube at NERA-ARU.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:55.880
Links in the show notes.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.380
Added wyбуск as witchens помощью EE синтеза-голоса,

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.500
подбор тем и анализ остаются за человеком.
